<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="rings-for-protection-warrior-tank">Rings for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78493/hardheart-ring">
<img alt="Hardheart Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardheart Ring</span></a> is the only available ilvl 410 ring with tank stats which makes it an automatic BiS for all tanks. It's also significantly better than all the other ilvl 410 rings in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> thanks to excellent secondary stats and a blue socket. <br/>The next best ring is the more DPS-oriented <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78432/curled-twilight-claw">
<img alt="Curled Twilight Claw" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_24.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curled Twilight Claw</span></a> by virtue of being another ilvl 410 ring with high stamina and mastery, and a secondary stat that isn't terrible. That being said, it's only a sidegrade to the ilvl 397 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77232/hardheart-ring">
<img alt="Hardheart Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardheart Ring</span></a> despite the item level difference, which would be preferred if this tank ring wasn't <b>unique-equipped</b>.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77112/signet-of-the-resolute">
<img alt="Signet of the Resolute" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of the Resolute</span></a> bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> is the second tank ring added with Phase 4 and, despite its lack of mastery, it slots right below the ilvl 397 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77232/hardheart-ring">
<img alt="Hardheart Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardheart Ring</span></a> which makes it a must-buy before tackling the heroic difficulty.<br/>
<br/>Although there are technically other ilvl 410 DPS-oriented rings that could be mentioned due to their high stamina or mastery, it would be frowned upon to contest DPS classes on their BiS rings when these are worse for a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> than the "free" <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77112/signet-of-the-resolute">
<img alt="Signet of the Resolute" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signet of the Resolute</span></a> and ilvl 384 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78498/hardheart-ring">
<img alt="Hardheart Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardheart Ring</span></a> that can be acquired with dungeon currencies.<div class="pad"></div>
