<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-protection-warrior-tank">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78003/indomitable-pride">
<img alt="Indomitable Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_rebirth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Pride</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77990/soulshifter-vortex">
<img alt="Soulshifter Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_cyclone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soulshifter Vortex</span></a> are basically the two best trinkets for the remainder of the game <b>in any version from ilvl 410 to ilvl 384</b>. They are amazing equip-and-forget trinkets with very high stamina ideal for all incoming damage types, paired with passive effects that you never have to think about. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78003/indomitable-pride">
<img alt="Indomitable Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_rebirth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Pride</span></a> in particular is the best emergency proc a tank could hope for at this late stage of the game when bosses hit like trucks. <br/>
<br/>The ilvl 384 versions of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77983/indomitable-pride">
<img alt="Indomitable Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_rebirth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Pride</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77970/soulshifter-vortex">
<img alt="Soulshifter Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_cyclone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soulshifter Vortex</span></a> can be acquired with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>s before your first raid and are a must-have as soon as possible, even if you already have the best trinkets from the last phase <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69138/spidersilk-spindle">
<img alt="Spidersilk Spindle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_firelands_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spidersilk Spindle</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69109/scales-of-life">
<img alt="Scales of Life" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_balanceofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scales of Life</span></a>. With these two ilvl 384 trinkets so easily available, it is fair to say all the other trinkets in the game are pretty much irrelevant. <br/>
<br/>Dodge trinkets such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=72900/veil-of-lies">
<img alt="Veil of Lies" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_fabric_ebonweave.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Veil of Lies</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77998/resolve-of-undying">
<img alt="Resolve of Undying" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_sharpeningstone_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Resolve of Undying</span></a> can have a niche usage against <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56427/warmaster-blackhorn">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Warmaster Blackhorn</span></a> to avoid <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=107567/brutal-strike">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_weaponmastery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Strike</span></a>'s incremental damage and tank for a little bit longer. But even in this ideal situation, they are only relevant as a second trinket next to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77983/indomitable-pride">
<img alt="Indomitable Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_rebirth.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Pride</span></a> until you acquire the ilvl 410 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77990/soulshifter-vortex">
<img alt="Soulshifter Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_cyclone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soulshifter Vortex</span></a> which has them both beat for survivability.<div class="pad"></div>
